diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: Campus DNS resolver on srv1 (BIND/named). Wireless access/gateway path (aswa1 → VLAN 40 → dswa2 SVI 10.6.0.1) is healthy.
- Mechanism: The laptop receives DNS server 10.5.0.4 (srv1). With recursion disabled, BIND returns REFUSED for any name it is not authoritative for. Applications that depend on DNS appear to “not work,” even though IP connectivity and default routing are fine.
- Localization: 
  • Laptop1 has IP 10.6.0.100/24, default via 10.6.0.1; it pings the gateway and other subnets successfully (pc1/pc2/pc3 OK) and reaches upstream (traceroute to 216.239.35.4 via 10.6.0.3 → 10.0.0.61 → r1 → 203.0.113.1).
